Hands-On SQL Practice: Database Creation & Queries
This week, I worked on strengthening my SQL fundamentals by practicing end-to-end operations:
🔹 Created a Database

CREATE DATABASE CompanyDB;
USE CompanyDB;
🔹 Created a Table

CREATE TABLE Employees (
    EmpID INT PRIMARY KEY,
    Name VARCHAR(50),
    Department VARCHAR(50),
    Salary INT
);
🔹 Inserted Records

INSERT INTO Employees VALUES
(1, 'Aarav Sharma', 'IT', 60000),
(2, 'Priya Mehta', 'HR', 50000),
(3, 'Rohit Singh', 'Finance', 65000),
(4, 'Ananya Gupta', 'Marketing', 55000),
(5, 'Karan Verma', 'IT', 70000);
🔹 Basic Queries

-- Retrieve all employees
SELECT * FROM Employees;

-- Retrieve IT department employees
SELECT * FROM Employees WHERE Department = 'IT';

-- Update salary
UPDATE Employees SET Salary = 75000 WHERE EmpID = 1;
💡 This exercise helped me brush up on data definition (DDL), data manipulation (DML), and querying techniques that are essential for database management and backend development.
